  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Revenue Mobilisation, Investment and Trade Programme (REMIT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Revenue Mobilisation, Investment and Trade (REMIT) is a 39-months (2021 &#x2013; 2025) programme funded by the UK&#x2019;s Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO). The programme provides technical assistance (TA) to Pakistan to implement reforms for strengthening macroeconomic stability and improving conditions for high and sustained growth, mutual prosperity, job creation and poverty reduction. The Programme works towards supporting the Government of Pakistan, its relevant ministries, institutions, and departments to strengthen revenue mobilisation reforms/initiatives; address investment environment challenges, facilitate trade and drive competitiveness by reducing trade barriers, and improve the macroeconomic policy and its management</narrative>
  </description>
